# gpio-edge-smoke

Wire the driver GPIO to the sensor GPIO named in main.cpp. On Linux, also
connect a 10 kOhm pull-up from the sensor to the board's I/O voltage. The
last check asks an operator to remove the jumper during a ten-second wait.

The application skips only when the first watch answers Unsupported. The
firmware image build cannot prove physical edge delivery; run it with the
fixture and a USB CDC console to see the verdict. Replace the jumper after
the manual step, including after a failure.

Exit codes:

| Code | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| 0 | All checks passed, or the edge facility was unavailable and skipped. |
| 1–2 | Initial watch or driver setup failed. |
| 3 | Rising/falling delivery or rejection check failed; inspect GPIO14/15. |
| 4–5 | Burst setup or watched-pin Busy contract failed. |
| 6–8 | Burst drive, delivery, or eventual clearing failed. |
| 9–13 | Immediate wait, quiet timeout, or unwatched take failed. |
| 14–17 | Manual wait setup, wait, read, or unwatch failed. |
| 18 | Sensor stayed low; check the jumper and pull-up. |
| 19 | Operator confirmed an in-window removal; edge was missed. |
| 20 | Removal timing was inconclusive or no answer arrived in 30 seconds. |
